{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q243354","formula":"CS₂","hill":"CS2","elements":["C","S"],"composition":{"C":1.0,"S":2.0},"names":{"en":"Carbon disulfide","ru":"Сероуглерод","uk":"Сірковуглець"},"descriptions":{"en":"Carbon disulfide (also spelled as carbon disulphide) is an inorganic compound with the chemical formula CS2 and structure S=C=S. It is also considered as the anhydride of thiocarbonic acid. It is a colorless, flammable, neurotoxic liquid that is used as a building block in organic synthesis. Pure carbon disulfide has a pleasant, ether- or chloroform-like odor, but commercial samples are usually yellowish and are typically contaminated with foul-smelling impurities.","ru":"Сульфи́д углеро́да(IV) (сероуглеро́д) — химическое вещество, бинарное соединение серы с углеродом. Высший сульфид углерода с формулой CS 2 {\\displaystyle {\\ce {CS2}}} .","uk":"Сірковуглець CS2 — неорганічна сполука вуглецю та сірки складу CS2. За звичайних умов являє собою прозору або жовтувату летку рідину з ефірним запахом. Використовується для синтезу штучних волокон, а також як розчинник."},"fame":51,"pubchemCid":6348,"mass":76.15,"charge":0,"smiles":"C(=S)=S","inchikey":"QGJOPFRUJISHPQ-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"methanedithione","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"6348","atoms":3,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-1.59,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"S"},{"x":1.59,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"S"},{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"C"}],"bonds":[[0,2,2],[1,2,2]]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q243354","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carbon_disulfide","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%A1%D0%B5%